    "id": "pqueue-4872154a",
    "title": "Replace in-memory secondary indexes with axon-esf typed keys",
    "description": "Replace ADR-010 raw length-prefixed byte index key encoding in crates/pqueue-projection with axon_esf typed index key helpers from axon-esf v0.3.2 for typed queues, while preserving legacy IndexSpec raw-byte behavior. Previous attempt landed typed keys but review found blockers: update_fields/set_entity_document None clears the stored entity and typed index membership even though None means leave unchanged; typed lookups through the old Vec\u003cVec\u003cu8\u003e\u003e API parse JSON ambiguously and reject string values like 123/true/null; legacy IndexSpec byte indexes regressed to lossy UTF-8 string semantics; typed indexes are attached only in MemoryBackend::create_queue, not InMemoryProjection::ensure_shard or objectlog projection construction/rebuild paths. Fix these before advancing. For this bead, keep legacy raw-byte lookup semantics intact; do not invent the final typed query API here beyond making the old raw API safe/explicit. In-scope files: crates/pqueue-projection/src/lib.rs, compose_impls if needed, memory/objectlog projection construction call sites, secondary index tests. Out-of-scope: relational SQL parity and public typed query API beyond non-ambiguous safe behavior.",
    "acceptance": "cargo fmt --check passes; cargo test -p pqueue secondary_indexes -- --nocapture passes; cargo test -p pqueue-projection --lib -- --nocapture passes; tests cover update_fields with entity None preserving typed index membership and stored entity; legacy IndexSpec arbitrary invalid UTF-8 byte values remain byte-exact and non-lossy; typed string lookup values that are valid JSON tokens (123, true, false, null) are either queryable correctly through a documented unambiguous path or rejected with a clear Invalid error pending pqueue-9a733f91, not silently mis-typed; typed indexes are attached in MemoryBackend and every in-memory projection/objectlog projection constructor or rebuild path that receives QueueDefinition; rg -n 'from_utf8_lossy|encode_index_key|with_typed_indexes|typed_index_specs|set_entity_document' crates/pqueue-projection/src crates/pqueue-memory/src crates/pqueue-objectlog/src crates/pqueue-server/src/object_log_sqlite.rs shows no production lossy legacy index encoding and all projection constructors carry typed indexes where QueueDefinition is available.",
    "parent": "pqueue-fc8ef1aa",
